{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 TT-303 ACID MACHINE \u8212- mono acid synth in the style of the TB-303. Tribute, no samples, no sample ROM, all model.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CONTROLS AS ON THE ORIGINAL TUNING semitones (-24..+24), plus FINE in cents (act immediately) CUTOFF filter frequency, ~100 Hz .. ~1 kHz, resonance raises it up to 2x RESONANCE filter feedback up to self-oscillation ENV MOD depth of the filter envelope, up to 5.2 octaves DECAY decay of the filter envelope, ~25 ms .. ~570 ms ACCENT level AND filter boost of the accent circuit WAVEFORM sawtooth / square\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MODEL DETAILS (after R. Whittle / Devil Fish / Open303 / Stinchcombe)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Filter: 4 TPT stages at the poles of the idealised TB-303 diode ladder denominator \{0.128/1.038/2.325/3.236\} \u8212- this makes the open transfer function exact. Level-dependent feedback k/(1+0.4|y|), 2x oversampled, 7-tap half-band decimation. Soft clip only at the master. Feedback HP 20 Hz, pole correction 1/(1+0.10*kRes).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Square: pitch-dependent duty ~0.5*sqrt(85 Hz/f) (after Burnett) and a lower level than saw -> different filter excitation. 1-sample PolyBLEP. The VCO runs freely.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Accent: own control latch + RC network (sweep capacitor charges via diode+R, discharges via the pot wiper; smoothed VCA path 47k x 0.033 uF). MEG time on accent = decay minimum.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Slide: RC time constant in log frequency space; the same note stays.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FX: delay/reverb bypassed at mix < 0.5 %. EQ OFF = true bypass.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab MIDI: notes are consumed, CC/pitchbend keep going.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 OPERATING MODES HOST Pure sound generator, played from the piano roll. Velocity >= threshold = accent, overlapping notes = slide. SEQ Internal 16-step sequencer, four pattern banks A-D with copy function, random and mutation, shuffle, gate length. Runs on the project timeline or free (FREE RUN). MIDI notes transpose the pattern (C2 = original pitch). MIDI OUT also sends the sequence out. All four banks travel with the project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Effect path: ahead of each of the three units \u8212- WaveShaper (Soft/Hard/ Fold/Fuzz), ping-pong delay, Freeverb reverb \u8212- sits an input EQ as a dual slider (lowcut left, highcut right, 0..20 kHz). After that compressor (-14 dB, 5:1) and master.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The input EQ only shapes what is sent into each effect; the dry signal runs alongside. On the drive the filtered band is distorted and the rest is added back undistorted \u8212- a raised lowcut takes the bass out of the DISTORTION, not out of the output.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIDI: THRU (header) passes INCOMING notes on, SEQ OUT (sequencer panel) sends the GENERATED sequence out \u8212- two sources, two switches. CC/pitchbend always pass through. In SEQ mode incoming notes are transpose commands.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 SURFACE after the Tim Techlor design kit: Core Black, Core White, Acid Green #39FF14, traces at a 45 degree angle with solder pads. Wordmark in Zilap Orion, if installed. Labels sans-serif (Segoe UI / Helvetica Neue / DejaVu Sans / Arial), numeric values monospaced (Consolas / DejaVu Sans Mono / Menlo / Courier New). Which of these is present the script measures itself. The front computes in a fixed design grid and scales to the window size \u8212- to enlarge, just drag the FX window open. HiDPI is honoured via gfx_ext_retina. All internal JSFX sliders are hidden ("-" before the name), operation is exclusively via the device front.\par}
}

